safix::card_pin_rejected

  × 11111111 refused the PIN, and the generator asked again. Nothing further
  │ was
  │ attempted.
  │ 
  │ One attempt, deliberately: a card allows three and a run that answered
  │ every prompt would spend all three on the same wrong PIN and block the
  │ card. The counter is at two rather than at zero.
  │ 
  │ If safix provisioned this card, its PIN is in custody — safix get
  │ 11111111's
  │ access entry — or in the password store beside it. If somebody else did,
  │ the PIN is theirs to supply.
  │ 
  │ A blocked PIN is unblocked with the PUK; a blocked PUK leaves the PIV
  │ applet resettable and every identity on it gone.
